@page "/architecture"
@inject IOptions<DemoOptions> Demo

<PageTitle>Architecture · Northstar</PageTitle>

<div class="page-head">
    <div>
        <h1 class="grad-text">Architecture</h1>
        <p class="lead">Why “LLM writes SQL” does not reach production – and what a governed Chat-with-Data pipeline looks like instead. The model proposes a structured intent; deterministic server code owns everything that touches data.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card accent-amber">
        <div class="card-head"><h2><span class="badge amber">Prototype</span> LLM → SQL → database</h2></div>
        <div class="flow proto">
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">1</span><div><b>User question</b><small>“How much revenue did we make in Q3 2026?”</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node llm"><span class="idx">2</span><div><b>LLM writes SQL</b><small>Prompt contains the schema; the model invents a definition of “revenue”.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node danger"><span class="idx">3</span><div><b>SQL is executed as-is</b><small>Service account with broad access · no catalog · no RLS · prompt injection goes straight through.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">4</span><div><b>A confident number</b><small>No definition, no lineage, no explanation. Finance disagrees two days later.</small></div></div>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:1rem">The prototype reads the synthetic order table directly – one implicit revenue definition, no governance layer, no row-level security.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card accent-cyan">
        <div class="card-head"><h2><span class="badge cyan">Production</span> governed pipeline</h2></div>
        <div class="flow prod">
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">1</span><div><b>Natural-language question</b><small>Plus conversation context (pending clarification, recent questions).</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node llm"><span class="idx">2</span><div><b>Azure OpenAI interprets</b><small>Temperature 0, strict JSON schema. The model never sees data and never writes a query.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">3</span><div><b>Structured intent</b><small>metric · dimensions · period · comparePeriod · filters · topN · visualization</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">4</span><div><b>Catalog check</b><small>Metric ids, dimensions, filter values and periods are validated against the server-owned Metric Catalog.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">5</span><div><b>Ambiguity detection</b><small>“revenue” → Gross / Net / Adjusted Net? Terms that map to several definitions are flagged.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">6</span><div><b>Clarification</b><small>The user picks the definition; the pending intent resumes with the chosen metric.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">7</span><div><b>Deterministic DAX builder</b><small>Only approved measures and columns; SUMMARIZECOLUMNS, TOPN, period filters – all generated by code.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">8</span><div><b>Execute Queries API with delegated identity</b><small>Power BI REST API, token acquired on behalf of the signed-in user → Fabric row-level security applies.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">9</span><div><b>Validated typed result</b><small>Rows, labels, warnings, truncation – mapped into a typed QueryResult, never raw JSON.</small></div></div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="flow-node"><span class="idx">10</span><div><b>Answer + visual + explanation</b><small>Definition, formula, owner, period, filters, data origin, security context. Every step is recorded in the Query Inspector.</small></div></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
    <div class="card-head"><h2>Fabric workspace – what the sample provisions</h2><span class="badge @(Demo.Value.ExecutionMode == ExecutionMode.Connected ? "cyan" : "amber")">currently: @Demo.Value.ExecutionMode</span></div>
    <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="card soft">
            <h3>Warehouse <span class="badge">yours</span></h3>
            <p class="muted small">A warehouse you choose or create; the provisioning tool adds the isolated schema <code class="inline">cwd</code> (star schema) with <code class="inline">cwd.FactFinanceAdjustment</code>, fed by the Excel ingestion step (or a Dataflow Gen2 in a real pipeline).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card soft">
            <h3>Prototype data source <span class="badge amber">ungoverned</span></h3>
            <p class="muted small">Used by <strong>Prototype Mode</strong>: direct access to the synthetic order table with one implicit revenue definition – deliberately simplified, no RLS, for comparison with Production Mode.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card soft accent-cyan">
            <h3>Semantic model <code class="inline">CWD-GovernedModel</code> <span class="badge cyan">deployed by the tool</span></h3>
            <p class="muted small">Used by <strong>Production Mode</strong>: published measures from the catalog (Gross, Net, Adjusted Net Revenue, Finance Adjustments…), RLS roles per region, Date table for period logic.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card soft" style="margin-top:1rem">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Mermaid source</h3><span class="badge">diagram</span></div>
    <pre class="code wrap" style="max-height:none">@MermaidSource</pre>
    <pre class="mermaid">@MermaidSource</pre>
</div>

@code {
    private const string MermaidSource = """
flowchart TD
    Q[Natural-language question] --> LLM[Azure OpenAI interprets<br/>strict JSON schema]
    LLM --> I[Structured intent]
    I --> C[Catalog check]
    C --> A{Ambiguous term?}
    A -- yes --> CL[Clarification: pick definition]
    CL --> C
    A -- no --> V{Valid?}
    V -- no --> R[Rejected with validation issues]
    V -- yes --> D[Deterministic DAX builder]
    D --> X[Execute Queries API<br/>delegated identity, RLS]
    X --> T[Validated typed result]
    T --> O[Answer + visual + explanation]
    O --> INS[(Query Inspector / audit)]
""";
}
